# UniVault wallet (Expo): copy to wallet/.env and adjust, then restart `npm start`.
#
# WARNING: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is compiled into the app and is PUBLIC: anyone who has
# the app can read it. Never put secrets (API keys, JWT secrets, passwords, private keys) here.
# An empty value means "not set".

# Base URL of the UniVault backend API, INCLUDING /api/v1, as reachable FROM THE PHONE.
#
# The phone cannot use "localhost": on a phone, localhost is the phone itself. Use one of:
#   - your PC's LAN IP address (PowerShell: `ipconfig`, the IPv4 address of your Wi-Fi
#     adapter), e.g. http://192.168.1.20:4000/api/v1 – phone and PC on the same Wi-Fi, and
#     Windows Firewall allowing inbound TCP 4000 (see wallet/README.md);
#   - or a tunnel to the backend (e.g. `ngrok http 4000`), e.g. https://<id>.ngrok-free.app/api/v1.
# The backend already listens on all network interfaces (app.listen(PORT) without a host).
#
# Next tasks (wallet redemption of credential offers): the backend's PUBLIC_BASE_URL (in
# backend/.env) must then use the SAME LAN address or tunnel, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:4000,
# because it becomes the OpenID4VCI credential_issuer inside the QR code the phone scans.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.x.x:4000/api/v1
